  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Suppose that $f(-4)=1$ and ${f}^{\u2032}(-4)=6.$ Using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=-4,$ estimate the value of $f(-3.8).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$f(-3.8)\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=-4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{\u2032}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(-4)+{f}^{\u2032}(-4)(x-(-4)) \\\\  & =1+6(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-3.8)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-3.8.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3.8) & \u2248L(-3.8) \\\\  & =1+6(-3.8+4) \\\\  & =1+6(0.2) \\\\  & =1+1.2 \\\\  & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
